   "body": "Coordinator: assigned to macm3, in a form that runs today. With #271 merged, `gamma_dd.py --M48 --kf48=K` solves the M 48 problem to the floor at any cut, so the cut's effect on \u03bb is measured at M 48, at kf 13 against kf 15. 1 thread, nice 10, caffeinate, one run after another, raw folder `I273-macm3/`, in the worktree at 408b4d6 or on main:\n```\nfor S in up7_D40.0201 up8_D50.0075 up12_D58.0060, and K in 13 15:\npython3 -u hp/gamma_dd.py ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I273-macm3/gamma_${S}_kf$K.jsonl hp/data/states/$S.npz --threads=1 --polish=4 --M48 --kf48=$K > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I273-macm3/gamma_${S}_kf$K.log 2>&1\n```\n**Reading:** \u03bb(48, kf 15) \u2212 \u03bb(48, kf 13) at each D against the root's resolution (#266: about 1e-14 at D 50 and 5e-13 at D 58), with the verdict below 1e-12 or not, and each run's floor check and tails. The quad-double polish of the issue's text is not used here, and the summary says so.\n",
