   "body": "## Closing summary (macm3, 2026-11-10 07:23 UTC)\n\n**The cut's effect on \u03bb at M 48 is below 1e-12 at D 40, 50 and 58, but at D 58 the kf 15 solve does not reach the floor and the difference sits at the root's resolution.**\n\n**What ran.** The coordinator's six `gamma_dd.py --M48 --kf48=K` runs one after another, as written, in the worktree at 408b4d6, one thread, nice 10, `caffeinate -is`. Five exited 0 and D 58 kf 15 exited 1 (floor check above its limit). The first runs were throttled while the Mac was on battery until 06:04 UTC. **The quad-double polish of the issue's text was not used**: the states are double-double with `--polish=4`, as the coordinator specified.\n\n| D | \u03bb(48, kf 15) \u2212 \u03bb(48, kf 13) | root's resolution | kf 13 floor, `est` | kf 15 floor, `est` | below 1e-12 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 40.02 | +1.33e-15 | 1e-14 (`find_lam`'s `xtol`) | ok, \u22123.8e-22 | ok, \u22123.3e-22 | yes |\n| 50.01 | \u22121.60e-14 | about 1e-14 (#266) | ok, \u22129.2e-20 | ok, \u22128.4e-16 | yes |\n| 58.01 | \u22124.93e-13 | about 5e-13 (#266) | ok, +2.0e-18 | **ABOVE**, \u22122.36e-15 | yes, by a factor 2 |\n\n| D | \u03bb(48, kf 13) | \u03bb(48, kf 15) | \\|F(48)\\| kf 13, kf 15 | \u0394(48) \u2212 \u0394(32), kf 13 / kf 15 | tails at kf 15 (centre, horizon) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 40.02 | 2.062779672619633 | 2.062779672619634 | 1.9e-26, 2.6e-26 | \u22126.5e-22 / +1.5e-15 | 1.7e-90, 1.3e-50 |\n| 50.01 | 2.0518437564334513 | 2.0518437564334353 | 4.4e-25, 5.1e-25 | \u22121.5e-20 / \u22122.2e-16 | 6.6e-109, 5.7e-43 |\n| 58.01 | 2.0455297614777623 | 2.045529761477269 | 1.4e-23, 2.3e-23 | \u22123.1e-18 / +1.1e-15 | 5.6e-121, 2.2e-37 |\n\nThe M 32 \u03bb of every record equals the old one bit for bit (2.0627796726196337, 2.051843756433441, 2.045529761477777).\n\n**Reading.**\n- D 40 and D 50: the differences, 1.3e-15 and \u22121.6e-14, are at or just above the root's resolution and 2 to 3 orders under 1e-12. Both floor checks pass.\n- D 58: \u22124.9e-13 is about one resolution (5e-13) and half the 1e-12 line. The kf 15 solve stops with `est` \u22122.36e-15, 2.4 times over the limit, so the difference is not read as a clean measurement of the cut. By #266's sensitivity, about 0.06 in \u03bb per unit of \u0394, that `est` moves \u03bb by about 1e-16; that is #266's figure at D 50 and is not measured here.\n- The kf 15 `est` grows with D (\u22123e-22, \u22128e-16, \u22122e-15) and so does the kf 15 horizon tail (1.3e-50, 5.7e-43, 2.2e-37). The cut makes the M 48 solve harder as D grows.\n- \u0394(48) at kf 15 differs from \u0394(32) at kf 13 by 1.5e-15, 2.2e-16 and 1.1e-15, so the cut moves \u0394 by about 1e-15 as well.\n- #290 shows the other side at D 61: there both M 48 solves at kf 13, 21 and 23 stop above the floor, with \u03bb shifts of about 1e-12.\n\n**Acceptance.** The verdict below 1e-12 is yes at all three D, with the D 58 caveat above.\n\n**Raw.** `I273-macm3/`, local commit d7f89ac of the raw-data clone, **not yet pushed** (SSH down).\n\n**Recommended tasks.**\n1. *Take D 58 kf 15 to the floor.* What: the same run with more Levenberg-Marquardt iterations, then kf 17. Why: the D 58 difference is at the root's resolution with a floor miss. Acceptance: floor ok at kf 15 and 17, and \u03bb(48, kf 15) \u2212 \u03bb(48, kf 13) with an error bar from the root's resolution. Depends on #273.\n2. *Measure the root's resolution at D 40 and D 58 directly.* What: repeat the kf 13 run of each with a changed `find_lam` bracket. Why: only D 50's resolution (#266) is measured, and the D 40 figure used here is `find_lam`'s `xtol`. Acceptance: the spread of \u03bb(48) over five brackets at each D. Depends on #266, #273.",
